Think: Build per_file_totals.txt by reading each filename from txt_file_list.txt, using wc to get line and word counts, and writing "filename, line_count, word_count, sum" for each file.

Act: bash

```bash
awk '{
  cmd = "wc -l \"" $0 "\"";
  cmd | getline res; close(cmd);
  split(res,a);
  l = a[1];
  cmd2 = "wc -w \"" $0 "\"";
  cmd2 | getline res2; close(cmd2);
  split(res2,b);
  w = b[1];
  sum = l + w;
  print $0", "l", " "w", " "sum
}' txt_file_list.txt > per_file_totals.txt
```

